# Assistant-configuration trees owned by the LOCAL TOOL, not by the repository.
#
# These are machine-installed per-agent configuration (editor/CLI assistant
# directories, tool-managed skill copies, and the OpenSpec CLI's own
# `.openspec-target` pointer). Committing them makes `git status` an
# unusable signal: every agent install dirties the tree with files nobody
# authored, which is exactly how real work gets missed in a diff.
#
# Repository-OWNED agent content is deliberately NOT matched by these rules
# and stays tracked: `.agents/skills/{continue-development,goal,harden}/`,
# `.claude/commands/goal.md`, `.kimi-code/AGENTS.md`, and
# `.opencode/commands/goal.md`. To add a new repository-owned agent file under
# one of these trees, add it with `git add -f <path>` — a deliberate,
# reviewable act, not an accident of a broad ignore rule. The
# credential-bearing exclusions above (`.kimi-code/local.toml`, `*.pem`,
# `*.key`, `.env*`) keep their explicit entries regardless of these rules.
.cline/
.clinerules/
.commandcode/
.cursor/
.devin/
.omp/
.pi/
.claude/skills/
.claude/commands/opsx/
.opencode/skills/
.opencode/commands/opsx-apply.md
.opencode/commands/opsx-archive.md
.opencode/commands/opsx-explore.md
.opencode/commands/opsx-propose.md
.opencode/commands/opsx-sync.md
.opencode/commands/opsx-update.md
.kimi-code/skills/
.agents/skills/.openspec-target
.agents/skills/openspec-apply-change/
.agents/skills/openspec-archive-change/
.agents/skills/openspec-explore/
.agents/skills/openspec-propose/
.agents/skills/openspec-sync-specs/
.agents/skills/openspec-update-change/

# External assistant / IDE local state
.workbuddy-ai/
# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

